\paragraph{How many features does each method need?}
\Cref{fig:ablation} reports the fraction of the true action-value difference that each critic reads, as the feature dimension grows.
FB reads none of it with up to three features, $41\%$ with four, and $96\%$ from five on.
\name{} reads $68\%$ with two features and all of it from three on.
\Cref{app:bottleneck-ablation} separates \name{}'s components: applying a softmax to the bilinear scores accounts for the difference, since a softmax fitted by squared error matches \name{}, while normalizing FB's target leaves it unchanged.

