\subsection{Performance across benchmarks}
\label{sec:exp-manipulation}

We next evaluate \name{} on 11 manipulation tasks from OGBench, MetaWorld, and ManiSkill, and locomotion tasks in DMC (\cref{tab:benchmarks}).
Dataset details are provided in \cref{app:data-mw-ms}.
\name{} achieves higher mean success than FB on every manipulation task, with average gains of $60.1$, $32.7$, and $14.0$ percentage points on OGBench, MetaWorld, and ManiSkill, respectively. It also exceeds HILP and RLDP on all 11 tasks.

Against the goal-conditioned baselines, \name{} achieves the highest mean success on nine tasks, including all three OGBench and all five ManiSkill tasks.
QRL has higher mean success on \texttt{bin-picking} and \texttt{box-close}, and on the MetaWorld average.
On OGBench, \name{} is conditioned on the task's goal state, as are the goal-conditioned baselines.

